WEBVTT

00:00:06.994 --> 00:00:08.427
Sammy!

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.327
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.427
Go!

00:00:14.161 --> 00:00:16.360
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:18.161
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:20.994 --> 00:00:23.293
This is dad's book.

00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:25.161
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off -

00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:28.861
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.927
I got to find dad. It's the
only think i can think about.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.094
Bethany: now i lay me down to sleep.

00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:41.293
I pray the lord my soul to keep.

00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:44.027
Thy angels watch me through the night

00:00:44.061 --> 00:00:46.794
And keep me safe till morning light.

00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:49.761
Amen.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.260
Night, monkeypuss.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.094
Daddy?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.161
Is mommy coming home?

00:01:07.761 --> 00:01:10.027
No, honey.

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:13.128
She's spending the night at
the hospital with your sister.

00:01:13.161 --> 00:01:14.460
Hey.

00:01:14.494 --> 00:01:16.627
You sleep tight now.

00:03:10.977 --> 00:03:14.177
Dean: yeah, you probably
missed something.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.344
Dude, i ran lexisnexis,
local police reports,

00:03:16.377 --> 00:03:18.644
Newspapers
- I couldn't find a single red flag.

00:03:18.677 --> 00:03:20.744
Are you sure you got
the coordinates right?

00:03:20.778 --> 00:03:21.878
Yeah, i double-Checked.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.210
It's fitchburg, wisconsin.

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:25.210
Dad wouldn't have sent us coordinates

00:03:25.244 --> 00:03:26.878
If it wasn't important, sammy.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.210
Well, i'm telling you, i looked,

00:03:28.244 --> 00:03:30.244
And all i could find was a
big, steamy pile of nothing.

00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:31.577
If dad's sending us
hunting for something,

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.644
I don't know what.

00:03:32.677 --> 00:03:34.144
Well, maybe he's gonna meet us there.

00:03:34.177 --> 00:03:37.344
Yeah, 'cause he's been so
easy to find up to this point.

00:03:37.377 --> 00:03:39.544
You're a real smartass, you know that?

00:03:39.577 --> 00:03:40.910
Don't worry.

00:03:40.943 --> 00:03:43.310
I'm sure there's something
in fitchburg worth killing.

00:03:43.344 --> 00:03:45.544
Yeah? What makes you so sure?

00:03:45.577 --> 00:03:48.744
Because i'm the oldest,
which means i'm always right.

00:03:48.778 --> 00:03:51.477
No, it doesn't. It totally does.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.611
Well, the waitress thinks

00:04:09.644 --> 00:04:12.778
That the local freemasons
are up to something sneaky,

00:04:12.811 --> 00:04:14.077
But other than that,

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.844
Nobody's heard about
anything weird going on.

00:04:16.878 --> 00:04:20.277
Dean, you got the time?

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.577
10 after 4:00.

00:04:22.611 --> 00:04:24.177
Why?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.344
What's wrong with this picture?

00:04:32.444 --> 00:04:35.677
School's out, isn't it?

00:04:35.711 --> 00:04:37.310
Yeah.

00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:41.811
So where is everybody?

00:04:41.844 --> 00:04:45.577
This place should be
crawling with kids right now.

00:04:59.344 --> 00:05:01.977
It sure is quiet out here.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.778
Yeah, it's a shame.

00:05:03.811 --> 00:05:05.077
Why is that?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.577
You know, kids getting
sick. It's a terrible thing.

00:05:08.611 --> 00:05:10.910
How many?

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:15.444
Just five or six, but
serious, hospital serious.

00:05:15.477 --> 00:05:18.177
A lot of parents are
getting pretty anxious.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.744
They think it's catching.

00:05:33.477 --> 00:05:35.844
Dude, dude, i am not using this i.D.

00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:37.010
Why not?

00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:39.077
Because it says "bikini
inspector" on it.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.043
Don't worry. She won't look that close.

00:05:41.077 --> 00:05:42.844
Hell, she won't even ask to see it.

00:05:42.878 --> 00:05:44.210
It's all about confidence, sammy.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.144
Hi.

00:05:47.177 --> 00:05:50.110
I'm dr. Jerry kaplan,
center for disease control.

00:05:50.144 --> 00:05:52.244
Can i see some i.D.?

00:05:55.177 --> 00:05:57.411
Yeah, of course.

00:05:59.744 --> 00:06:02.644
Now, could you direct me
to the pediatrics ward?

00:06:02.677 --> 00:06:06.144
Okay, just go down that hall,
turn left, up the stairs.

00:06:06.177 --> 00:06:07.644
You'll see them.

00:06:07.677 --> 00:06:09.477
Right. Thank you.

00:06:09.511 --> 00:06:11.611
See? Told you it would work.

00:06:11.644 --> 00:06:14.411
Follow me. It's upstairs.

00:06:48.677 --> 00:06:50.010
Sam: dean.

00:06:59.344 --> 00:07:01.377
Thanks for seeing us, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:01.411 --> 00:07:03.277
Oh, i'm glad you guys are here.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.677
I was just about to call the cdc myself.

00:07:05.711 --> 00:07:07.444
How did you find out anyway?

00:07:07.477 --> 00:07:09.644
Oh, some g.P. - I
forget his name -

00:07:09.677 --> 00:07:12.677
He called atlanta and must
have beat you to the punch.

00:07:12.711 --> 00:07:15.477
So you say you got six cases so far?

00:07:15.511 --> 00:07:17.878
Yeah, in five weeks.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.411
At first i thought it
was bacterial pneumonia,

00:07:20.444 --> 00:07:21.544
Not that newsworthy.

00:07:21.577 --> 00:07:23.444
But now...

00:07:23.477 --> 00:07:25.611
Now, what?

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:27.977
The kids aren't
responding to antibiotics.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.277
Their white-Cell
counts keep going down.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:33.010
Their immune systems just
aren't doing their job.

00:07:33.043 --> 00:07:35.844
It's like their bodies are wearing out.

00:07:35.878 --> 00:07:37.444
Betty: excuse me, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:37.477 --> 00:07:39.244
You ever see anything like this before?

00:07:39.277 --> 00:07:40.411
Never this severe.

00:07:40.444 --> 00:07:42.943
The way it spreads
- That's a new one for me.

00:07:42.977 --> 00:07:44.210
What do you mean?

00:07:44.244 --> 00:07:45.744
It works its way through families,

00:07:45.778 --> 00:07:48.977
But only the children,
one sibling after another.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:52.477
You mind if we interview
a few of the kids?

00:07:52.511 --> 00:07:54.644
They're not conscious.

00:07:54.677 --> 00:07:56.811
None of them?

00:07:56.844 --> 00:07:58.644
No.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:01.844
Can we talk to the parents?

00:08:03.277 --> 00:08:05.210
If you think it'll help.

00:08:05.244 --> 00:08:08.811
Yeah, yeah. Who was your
most recent admission?

00:08:08.844 --> 00:08:11.077
I should get back to my girls.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.344
We understand that,

00:08:12.377 --> 00:08:15.077
And we really appreciate
you talking to us.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:17.144
Now, you say mary's the oldest?

00:08:17.177 --> 00:08:18.377
13.

00:08:18.411 --> 00:08:20.577
Okay, and she came down
with it first, right?

00:08:20.611 --> 00:08:21.677
And then...

00:08:21.711 --> 00:08:23.844
Bethany the next night.

00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:25.744
Within 24 hours?

00:08:25.778 --> 00:08:28.511
I guess.

00:08:28.544 --> 00:08:31.611
Look, i already went through
all this with the doctor.

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:33.644
Right. Just a few more
questions, if you don't mind.

00:08:33.677 --> 00:08:35.577
How do you think they caught pneumonia?

00:08:35.611 --> 00:08:37.778
Were they out in the
cold, anything like that?

00:08:37.811 --> 00:08:39.943
No, we think it was an open window.

00:08:39.977 --> 00:08:42.277
Both times?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:45.878
The first time, i don't really remember,

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.444
But the second time for sure,

00:08:47.477 --> 00:08:50.477
And i know i closed it
before i put bethany to bed.

00:08:50.511 --> 00:08:52.010
So you think she opened it?

00:08:52.043 --> 00:08:54.577
It's a second-Story window, no ledge.

00:08:54.611 --> 00:08:56.177
No one else could have.

00:09:00.744 --> 00:09:03.310
You know this might not
be anything supernatural.

00:09:03.344 --> 00:09:04.943
It might just be pneumonia.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.210
Maybe. Or maybe something
opened that window.

00:09:07.244 --> 00:09:10.110
I don't know, man. Look, dad
sent us down here for a reason.

00:09:10.144 --> 00:09:12.444
I think we might be
barking up the right tree.

00:09:12.477 --> 00:09:13.544
I'll tell you one thing.

00:09:13.577 --> 00:09:14.544
What?

00:09:14.577 --> 00:09:16.310
That guy we just talked to -

00:09:16.344 --> 00:09:19.110
I'm betting it'll be a
while before he goes home.

00:09:28.744 --> 00:09:31.177
You got anything over there?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.878
No, nothing.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.244
Yeah, me neither.

00:09:46.878 --> 00:09:48.344
Hey, dean.

00:09:48.377 --> 00:09:50.110
Dean: yeah?

00:09:51.611 --> 00:09:56.377
You were right. It's not pneumonia.

00:10:00.144 --> 00:10:02.310
It's rotted.

00:10:06.244 --> 00:10:08.844
What the hell leaves
a handprint like that?

00:10:12.177 --> 00:10:13.910
<i>Man: cheetara.</i>

00:10:13.943 --> 00:10:15.110
<i>Woman: i am sorry to wake you,</i>

00:10:15.144 --> 00:10:16.544
<i>But jaga bids me to bring you to him.</i>

00:10:16.577 --> 00:10:18.577
John: all right.

00:10:19.611 --> 00:10:21.177
You know the drill, dean.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:23.511
If anyone calls, you don't pick up.

00:10:23.544 --> 00:10:26.878
If it's me, i'll ring
once and then call back.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.244
You got that?

00:10:28.277 --> 00:10:31.577
Mm-Hmm. Don't answer the phone
unless it rings once first.

00:10:31.611 --> 00:10:34.210
Come on, dude. Look alive.
This stuff's important.

00:10:34.244 --> 00:10:35.344
I know, it's just,

00:10:35.377 --> 00:10:37.811
We've done it like a million times,

00:10:37.844 --> 00:10:39.644
And you know i'm not stupid.

00:10:39.677 --> 00:10:41.811
I know you're not, but
it only takes one mistake.

00:10:41.844 --> 00:10:43.210
You got that?

00:10:43.244 --> 00:10:46.611
<i>It's important that he join
jaga on the flight deck.</i>

00:10:46.644 --> 00:10:49.210
All right, if i'm not
back sunday night...

00:10:49.244 --> 00:10:50.611
Call pastor jim.

00:10:52.943 --> 00:10:55.511
Lock the doors and
windows, close the shades,

00:10:55.544 --> 00:10:56.744
And most important -

00:10:56.778 --> 00:10:58.310
Watch out for sammy.

00:10:58.344 --> 00:11:00.677
<i>Responsible for lion-O's
welfare, snarf is.</i>

00:11:00.711 --> 00:11:01.943
I know.

00:11:01.977 --> 00:11:03.611
All right, if something
tries to bust in...

00:11:03.644 --> 00:11:06.611
Shoot first, ask questions later.

00:11:06.644 --> 00:11:08.744
That's my man.

00:11:12.711 --> 00:11:14.010
<i>What's up, jaga?</i>

00:11:14.043 --> 00:11:15.110
<i>Come closer.</i>

00:11:19.943 --> 00:11:22.611
<i>What's happening to her?</i>

00:11:24.544 --> 00:11:26.411
<i>What was that?</i>

00:11:26.444 --> 00:11:29.010
Dean: i know why dad sent us here.

00:11:33.744 --> 00:11:35.844
He's faced this thing before.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:41.778
He wants us to finish the job.

00:12:04.183 --> 00:12:05.884
So what the hell is a shtriga?

00:12:05.917 --> 00:12:07.817
It's kind of like a witch, i think.

00:12:07.851 --> 00:12:09.484
I don't know much about them.

00:12:09.517 --> 00:12:11.484
Well, i've never heard of it,

00:12:11.517 --> 00:12:13.517
And it's not in dad's journal.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:16.183
Dad hunted one in fort
douglas, wisconsin,

00:12:16.217 --> 00:12:17.651
About 16, 17 years ago.

00:12:17.684 --> 00:12:20.517
You were there. You don't remember? No.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.018
I guess he caught wind that
the thing's in fitchburg now

00:12:23.051 --> 00:12:24.517
And kicked us the coordinates.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.784
So wait, this... shtriga.

00:12:26.817 --> 00:12:28.751
Right, you think it's the
same one dad hunted before?

00:12:28.784 --> 00:12:31.283
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:33.317
If dad went after it, why
is it still breathing air?

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.484
Because it got away.

00:12:34.517 --> 00:12:35.617
Got away?

00:12:35.651 --> 00:12:37.018
Yeah, sammy, it happens.

00:12:37.051 --> 00:12:38.217
Not very often.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.517
I don't know what to tell you.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.384
Maybe dad didn't have
his wheaties that morning.

00:12:41.417 --> 00:12:43.217
What else do you remember?

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:45.450
Nothing. I was a kid, all right?

00:12:55.217 --> 00:12:56.851
King or two queens?

00:12:56.884 --> 00:12:58.450
Two queens.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.118
Yeah, i bet.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.317
What'd you say?

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.283
Nice car.

00:13:07.317 --> 00:13:09.450
Hi. Checking in?

00:13:09.484 --> 00:13:10.684
Yeah.

00:13:10.717 --> 00:13:14.250
Uh, do me a favor. Go get
your brother some dinner.

00:13:14.283 --> 00:13:16.051
I'm helping a guest.

00:13:19.684 --> 00:13:21.851
Two queens.

00:13:23.984 --> 00:13:25.283
Funny kid.

00:13:25.317 --> 00:13:27.150
Oh, yeah, he thinks so.

00:13:27.183 --> 00:13:28.917
Will that be cash or credit?

00:13:28.951 --> 00:13:30.550
Do you take mastercard? Mm-Hmm.

00:13:30.584 --> 00:13:31.584
Perfect.

00:13:31.617 --> 00:13:32.684
There you go.

00:13:32.717 --> 00:13:35.118
Thank you.

00:13:50.984 --> 00:13:53.584
When's dad gonna get back?

00:13:53.617 --> 00:13:55.118
Tomorrow.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.350
When?

00:13:56.384 --> 00:13:57.384
I don't know.

00:13:57.417 --> 00:13:59.250
He usually comes in late, though.

00:13:59.283 --> 00:14:01.018
Now, eat your dinner.

00:14:01.051 --> 00:14:03.283
I'm sick of "scabetti-Os."

00:14:03.317 --> 00:14:05.917
Well, you're the one who wanted them.

00:14:05.951 --> 00:14:07.350
I want lucky charms.

00:14:07.384 --> 00:14:08.951
There's no more lucky charms.

00:14:08.984 --> 00:14:10.250
I saw the box.

00:14:10.283 --> 00:14:11.550
Okay, maybe there is,

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:14.150
But there's only enough
left for one bowl,

00:14:14.183 --> 00:14:15.751
And i haven't had any yet.

00:14:39.517 --> 00:14:41.951
Do you want the prize?

00:14:41.984 --> 00:14:44.384
Sir?

00:14:46.183 --> 00:14:48.217
Thanks.

00:14:58.851 --> 00:15:00.517
Well, you were right.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:04.283
It wasn't very easy to
find, but you were right.

00:15:04.317 --> 00:15:06.784
A shtriga is a kind of witch.

00:15:06.817 --> 00:15:08.051
They're albanian,

00:15:08.084 --> 00:15:11.018
But legends about them
date back to ancient rome.

00:15:11.051 --> 00:15:13.118
They feed off of spiritus vitae.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.784
Spirit what?

00:15:14.817 --> 00:15:16.084
Vitae. It's latin.

00:15:16.118 --> 00:15:18.183
It translates to "breath of life,"

00:15:18.217 --> 00:15:21.517
Kind of like your life force or essence.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.517
Didn't the doctor say the
kids' bodies were wearing out?

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:25.484
It's a thought.

00:15:25.517 --> 00:15:26.951
You know, she takes your vitality,

00:15:26.984 --> 00:15:29.118
Maybe your immunity goes to
hell, pneumonia takes hold.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:32.350
Anyway, shtrigas can feed
off anyone, but they prefer -

00:15:32.384 --> 00:15:34.118
Children.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.384
Yeah.

00:15:35.417 --> 00:15:37.484
Probably because they
have stronger life force.

00:15:37.517 --> 00:15:41.118
And get this
- Shtrigas are invulnerable

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:43.717
To all weapons devised by god and man.

00:15:43.751 --> 00:15:45.951
No, that's not right.

00:15:45.984 --> 00:15:49.450
She's vulnerable when she feeds.

00:15:49.484 --> 00:15:50.484
What?

00:15:50.517 --> 00:15:52.450
If you catch her when she's eating,

00:15:52.484 --> 00:15:55.018
You can blast her with
consecrated wrought irons,

00:15:55.051 --> 00:15:56.884
Buckshots or rounds i think.

00:15:56.917 --> 00:15:58.550
How do you know that?

00:15:58.584 --> 00:16:01.384
Dad told me. I remember.

00:16:01.417 --> 00:16:03.817
Oh.

00:16:03.851 --> 00:16:07.884
So, uh, anything else
dad might have mentioned?

00:16:07.917 --> 00:16:10.217
No, that's it.

00:16:12.283 --> 00:16:14.384
What?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.417
Nothing.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:22.250
Okay, so, assuming we
can kill it when it eats,

00:16:22.283 --> 00:16:24.084
We've still got to find the thing first,

00:16:24.118 --> 00:16:25.617
Which ain't gonna be a cakewalk.

00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:28.051
Shtrigas take on a human
disguise when they're not hunting.

00:16:28.084 --> 00:16:29.751
What kind of human disguise?

00:16:29.784 --> 00:16:31.584
Historically, something innocuous.

00:16:31.617 --> 00:16:34.417
It could be anything, but it's
usually a feeble old woman,

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.450
Which may be how the witches-As-
Old-Crones legend got started.

00:16:37.484 --> 00:16:38.550
Hang on.

00:16:38.584 --> 00:16:39.651
What?

00:16:41.651 --> 00:16:42.884
Check this out.

00:16:42.917 --> 00:16:45.084
I marked down all the
addresses of the victims.

00:16:45.118 --> 00:16:47.118
Now, these are the houses
that have been hit so far,

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.350
And dead center -

00:16:48.384 --> 00:16:50.584
The hospital.

00:16:50.617 --> 00:16:53.751
When we were there, i saw
a patient, an old woman.

00:16:53.784 --> 00:16:55.183
An old person, huh?

00:16:55.217 --> 00:16:56.250
Yeah.

00:16:56.283 --> 00:16:57.350
In the hospital?

00:16:57.384 --> 00:16:59.417
Whew! Better call the coast guard.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.751
Well, listen, smartass,

00:17:00.784 --> 00:17:03.417
She had an inverted
cross hanging on her wall.

00:17:18.484 --> 00:17:20.651
Betty: good night, dr. Hydaker.

00:17:20.684 --> 00:17:22.217
See you tomorrow, betty.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.350
Try to get some sleep, aaron.

00:17:30.384 --> 00:17:31.784
Come on.

00:18:33.183 --> 00:18:35.384
Who the hell are you?

00:18:35.417 --> 00:18:36.684
Who's there?

00:18:38.817 --> 00:18:40.951
You trying to steal my stuff?

00:18:40.984 --> 00:18:42.851
They're always stealing around here.

00:18:42.884 --> 00:18:45.684
No, ma'am, we're
maintenance. We're sorry.

00:18:45.717 --> 00:18:47.317
We thought you were sleeping.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.051
Ah, nonsense.

00:18:49.084 --> 00:18:51.384
I was sleeping with my peepers open.

00:18:54.851 --> 00:18:57.817
And fix that crucifix, would you?

00:18:57.851 --> 00:19:01.317
I've asked four damn times already.

00:19:58.707 --> 00:20:02.007
"I was sleeping with my peepers open."

00:20:02.041 --> 00:20:05.341
I almost smoked that old gal, i swear.

00:20:05.374 --> 00:20:06.774
It's not funny.

00:20:07.801 --> 00:20:10.034
Oh, man, you should have
seen your face, dean.

00:20:10.067 --> 00:20:12.667
Oh, yeah, laugh it on, man.
We're back to square one.

00:20:15.234 --> 00:20:17.933
Hang on.

00:20:26.567 --> 00:20:29.200
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:29.234 --> 00:20:32.134
My brother's sick.

00:20:32.167 --> 00:20:33.301
The little guy?

00:20:33.334 --> 00:20:35.200
Pneumonia.

00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:37.668
He's in the hospital.

00:20:39.067 --> 00:20:40.800
It's my fault.

00:20:40.833 --> 00:20:42.501
No, come on. How?

00:20:43.668 --> 00:20:46.267
I should have made sure
the window was latched.

00:20:46.301 --> 00:20:48.501
He wouldn't have gotten pneumonia

00:20:48.534 --> 00:20:50.167
If the window was latched.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.167
Listen to me.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:21:00.634
I can promise you that this
is not your fault, okay?

00:21:00.668 --> 00:21:03.100
It's my job to look after him.

00:21:09.933 --> 00:21:11.334
Michael.

00:21:13.768 --> 00:21:16.334
Turn on the "no vacancy"
sign while i'm gone.

00:21:16.367 --> 00:21:18.100
I've got denise covering room service,

00:21:18.134 --> 00:21:19.200
So don't bother with the rooms.

00:21:19.234 --> 00:21:20.567
I'm going with you. Not now, michael.

00:21:20.601 --> 00:21:21.701
But i got to see asher.

00:21:21.734 --> 00:21:23.167
Dean: hey, michael.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.534
Hey.

00:21:24.567 --> 00:21:27.334
I know how you feel.
I'm a big brother, too.

00:21:27.367 --> 00:21:30.067
But you got to go easy on
your mom right now, okay?

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:31.267
Aw, damn it.

00:21:31.301 --> 00:21:32.567
I got it.

00:21:32.601 --> 00:21:35.334
Thanks. You're in no condition to drive.

00:21:35.367 --> 00:21:38.100
Why don't you let me give
you a lift to the hospital?

00:21:38.134 --> 00:21:39.434
No, no, i couldn't possibly -

00:21:39.467 --> 00:21:43.067
No, no trouble. I insist.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.000
Be good.

00:21:57.668 --> 00:21:59.401
We're gonna kill this thing.

00:21:59.434 --> 00:22:01.501
I want it dead. You hear me?

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:21.134
Dean: hey.

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:22.567
Hey, how's the kid?

00:22:22.601 --> 00:22:25.034
He's not good. Where you at?

00:22:25.067 --> 00:22:26.601
I'm at the library,

00:22:26.634 --> 00:22:29.167
Trying to find out as much
as i can about this shtriga.

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:30.833
Yeah, what do you got?

00:22:30.867 --> 00:22:32.067
Well, bad news.

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.301
I started with fort douglas

00:22:34.334 --> 00:22:36.501
Around the time you said dad was there.

00:22:36.534 --> 00:22:37.768
And?

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:38.933
Same deal.

00:22:38.967 --> 00:22:42.334
Before that, there was ogdenville.

00:22:42.367 --> 00:22:46.234
Before that, north
haverbrook and brockway.

00:22:46.267 --> 00:22:49.967
Every 15 to 20 years,
it hits a new town.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.434
Dean, this thing is just
getting started in fitchburg.

00:22:53.467 --> 00:22:56.367
In all these other places,
it goes on for months,

00:22:56.401 --> 00:22:59.501
Dozens of kids, before the
shtriga finally moves on.

00:22:59.534 --> 00:23:03.100
Kids just languish in
comas, and then they die.

00:23:03.134 --> 00:23:05.301
How far back does this thing go?

00:23:05.334 --> 00:23:06.467
I don't know.

00:23:06.501 --> 00:23:09.167
The earliest mention i
could find is this place

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.668
Called black river
falls back in the 1890s.

00:23:11.701 --> 00:23:14.501
Talk about a horror show.

00:23:16.234 --> 00:23:18.501
Whoa.

00:23:18.534 --> 00:23:19.534
Sam?

00:23:19.567 --> 00:23:21.000
Hold on.

00:23:21.034 --> 00:23:23.367
I'm looking at a photograph right now

00:23:23.401 --> 00:23:26.601
Of a bunch of doctors
standing around a kid's bed.

00:23:26.634 --> 00:23:29.501
One of the doctors is hydaker.

00:23:29.534 --> 00:23:31.067
And?

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:34.334
And this picture was taken in 1893.

00:23:34.367 --> 00:23:36.534
You sure?

00:23:36.567 --> 00:23:38.134
Yeah.

00:23:38.167 --> 00:23:40.634
Yeah, absolutely.

00:23:59.134 --> 00:24:03.334
Don't worry. Your son's in good hands.

00:24:03.367 --> 00:24:06.601
I'm gonna take care of him.

00:24:06.634 --> 00:24:09.567
So what's the cdc come up with so far?

00:24:09.601 --> 00:24:12.100
We're still working on a few theories.

00:24:12.134 --> 00:24:14.701
You'll know something as soon as we do.

00:24:14.734 --> 00:24:18.167
Well, nothing's more important
to me than these kids.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:19.167
Hmm.

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:21.534
Just let me know if i can help.

00:24:21.567 --> 00:24:24.768
I'll do that.

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:29.534
Sam: we should have
thought of this before.

00:24:29.567 --> 00:24:32.000
Doctor's a perfect
disguise. You're trusted.

00:24:32.034 --> 00:24:33.900
You can control the whole thing.

00:24:33.933 --> 00:24:37.933
Huh. That son of a bitch.

00:24:37.967 --> 00:24:40.000
I'm surprised you didn't
draw on him right there.

00:24:40.034 --> 00:24:43.000
Yeah, well...

00:24:43.034 --> 00:24:45.000
First of all,

00:24:45.034 --> 00:24:46.967
I'm not gonna open fire in
a freakin' pediatrics ward.

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.668
Good call.

00:24:48.701 --> 00:24:50.267
Second, it wouldn't have done any good

00:24:50.301 --> 00:24:51.668
Because the bastard's bulletproof

00:24:51.701 --> 00:24:53.267
Unless he's chowing down on something.

00:24:53.301 --> 00:24:54.501
And third, i wasn't packing,

00:24:54.534 --> 00:24:56.067
Which is probably a really good thing

00:24:56.100 --> 00:24:58.200
'Cause i probably would have
just burned a clip in him

00:24:58.234 --> 00:24:59.634
Off of principle alone.

00:24:59.668 --> 00:25:02.234
You're getting wise
in your old age, dean.

00:25:02.267 --> 00:25:03.467
You're damn right.

00:25:03.501 --> 00:25:06.100
'Cause now i know how
we're gonna get it.

00:25:06.134 --> 00:25:08.134
What do you mean?

00:25:08.167 --> 00:25:10.000
The shtriga
- It works through siblings, right?

00:25:10.034 --> 00:25:11.134
Right.

00:25:11.167 --> 00:25:12.534
Well, last night...

00:25:12.567 --> 00:25:13.768
It went after asher.

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:15.701
Tonight it's probably
gonna come after michael.

00:25:15.734 --> 00:25:16.867
Then we got to get him out of here.

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:19.167
No. No, that would blow the whole deal.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:20.668
What? Yeah.

00:25:20.701 --> 00:25:23.100
Then you want to use the kid as bait?

00:25:24.167 --> 00:25:26.933
Are you nuts? No. Forget it.
That's out of the question.

00:25:26.967 --> 00:25:29.467
Sam, it's the only way
- If this thing disappears,

00:25:29.501 --> 00:25:31.800
It could be years before
we get another chance.

00:25:31.833 --> 00:25:33.567
Michael's a kid, and
i'm not gonna dangle him

00:25:33.601 --> 00:25:35.334
In front of that thing
like a worm on a hook.

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:37.334
Dad did not send me here to walk away.

00:25:37.367 --> 00:25:39.534
<i>Send you here? He didn't send you here.</i>

00:25:39.567 --> 00:25:41.768
<i>He sent us here. This
isn't about you, sam.</i>

00:25:41.800 --> 00:25:43.601
I'm the one that screwed
up. It's my fault.

00:25:43.634 --> 00:25:45.701
There's no telling how
many kids have gotten hurt

00:25:45.734 --> 00:25:46.833
Because of me.

00:25:46.867 --> 00:25:50.434
What are you saying,
dean? How is it your fault?

00:25:56.234 --> 00:25:57.668
Dean.

00:25:57.701 --> 00:26:00.933
You've been hiding
something from the get-Go.

00:26:00.967 --> 00:26:03.601
Since when does dad bail on a hunt?

00:26:03.634 --> 00:26:06.668
Since when does he
let something get away?

00:26:06.701 --> 00:26:11.900
Now, talk to me, man.
Tell me what's going on.

00:26:21.467 --> 00:26:24.234
Fort douglas, wisconsin.

00:26:24.267 --> 00:26:27.267
It was the third night
in this crap room,

00:26:27.301 --> 00:26:29.900
And i was climbing the walls, man.

00:26:29.933 --> 00:26:31.734
I needed to get some air.

00:26:31.768 --> 00:26:33.367
<i>...if ever i saw one.</i>

00:26:33.401 --> 00:26:35.000
<i>Command performance.</i>

00:27:01.933 --> 00:27:03.267
Hey, kid.

00:27:04.434 --> 00:27:06.434
We're closing up.

00:28:09.833 --> 00:28:11.134
Get out of the way!

00:28:21.467 --> 00:28:25.701
Sammy. Sammy. Sammy.

00:28:25.734 --> 00:28:27.000
You okay?

00:28:27.034 --> 00:28:29.768
Sam: dad, what's going on?

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:31.634
Are you all right?

00:28:35.234 --> 00:28:38.634
What happened?

00:28:38.668 --> 00:28:40.701
I
- I just went out.

00:28:40.734 --> 00:28:42.401
What?

00:28:42.434 --> 00:28:45.067
J
- Just for a second. I'm sorry.

00:28:45.100 --> 00:28:47.467
I told you not to leave this room.

00:28:47.501 --> 00:28:50.467
I told you not to let
him out of your sight.

00:29:02.668 --> 00:29:06.933
Dad just grabbed us and booked,

00:29:06.967 --> 00:29:12.501
Dropped us off at pastor
jim's about three hours away.

00:29:12.534 --> 00:29:15.301
By the time he got back to fort douglas,

00:29:15.334 --> 00:29:17.200
The shtriga had disappeared.

00:29:17.234 --> 00:29:19.467
It was just gone.

00:29:22.501 --> 00:29:26.668
It never resurfaced until now.

00:29:26.701 --> 00:29:29.668
Dad never spoke about it again.

00:29:29.701 --> 00:29:32.701
I didn't ask.

00:29:32.734 --> 00:29:35.234
But he, uh...

00:29:37.401 --> 00:29:42.501
He looked at me different,
you know, which was worse.

00:29:42.534 --> 00:29:44.000
Not that i blame him.

00:29:44.034 --> 00:29:46.900
He gave me an order,
and i didn't listen,

00:29:46.933 --> 00:29:49.067
And i almost got you killed.

00:29:49.100 --> 00:29:50.501
You were just a kid.

00:29:50.534 --> 00:29:54.501
Don't.

00:29:54.534 --> 00:29:59.034
Dad knew this was
unfinished business for me.

00:29:59.067 --> 00:30:02.267
He sent me here to finish it.

00:30:04.334 --> 00:30:08.134
But using michael
- I don't know, dean.

00:30:08.167 --> 00:30:11.367
I mean, how about one of
us hides under the cover?

00:30:11.401 --> 00:30:14.267
You know, we'll be the bait.

00:30:14.301 --> 00:30:17.267
No, that won't work.

00:30:17.301 --> 00:30:20.301
It's got to get close
enough to feed. It'll see us.

00:30:22.867 --> 00:30:25.367
Believe me, i don't like it,
but it's got to be the kid.

00:30:30.967 --> 00:30:32.933
Michael: you're crazy!

00:30:32.967 --> 00:30:35.567
Just go away or i'm calling the cops.

00:30:35.601 --> 00:30:37.634
Hang on a second. Just listen to me.

00:30:37.668 --> 00:30:40.134
You have to believe me, okay?

00:30:40.167 --> 00:30:41.734
This thing came through the window

00:30:41.768 --> 00:30:42.933
And attacked your brother.

00:30:45.501 --> 00:30:46.567
I've seen it.

00:30:46.601 --> 00:30:48.100
I know what it looks like

00:30:48.134 --> 00:30:50.601
'Cause it attacked my brother once, too.

00:30:57.833 --> 00:30:59.768
This thing -

00:30:59.800 --> 00:31:02.434
Is it, like...

00:31:02.467 --> 00:31:07.000
It has this long, black robe?

00:31:07.034 --> 00:31:09.267
You saw it last night, didn't you?

00:31:09.301 --> 00:31:13.267
I thought i was having a nightmare.

00:31:15.334 --> 00:31:19.301
I'd give anything not to tell you this,

00:31:19.334 --> 00:31:21.401
But sometimes nightmares are real.

00:31:21.434 --> 00:31:24.534
<i>So why are you telling me?</i>

00:31:24.567 --> 00:31:26.334
Because we need your help.

00:31:26.367 --> 00:31:27.734
My help?

00:31:27.768 --> 00:31:32.501
We can kill it, me and
him. It's what we do.

00:31:32.534 --> 00:31:34.567
But we can't do it without you.

00:31:34.601 --> 00:31:37.800
What? No.

00:31:37.833 --> 00:31:39.534
Michael, listen to me.

00:31:39.567 --> 00:31:41.301
This thing hurt asher,

00:31:41.334 --> 00:31:44.534
And it's gonna keep hurting
kids unless we stop it.

00:31:44.567 --> 00:31:46.000
Do you understand me?

00:31:48.701 --> 00:31:51.634
Well, that went crappy. Now what?

00:31:51.668 --> 00:31:52.833
What did you expect?

00:31:52.867 --> 00:31:55.434
You can't ask an adult
to do something like that,

00:31:55.467 --> 00:31:57.167
Much less a kid.

00:32:05.401 --> 00:32:08.234
If you kill it, will asher get better?

00:32:13.034 --> 00:32:16.567
Honestly, we don't know.

00:32:19.601 --> 00:32:22.501
You said you're a big brother.

00:32:22.534 --> 00:32:24.734
Yeah.

00:32:24.768 --> 00:32:26.601
You'd take care of your little brother?

00:32:26.634 --> 00:32:30.467
You'd do anything for him?

00:32:30.501 --> 00:32:32.734
Yeah, i would.

00:32:34.634 --> 00:32:38.434
Me too.

00:32:38.467 --> 00:32:39.833
I'll help.

00:33:00.970 --> 00:33:02.604
This camera has night vision on it,

00:33:02.638 --> 00:33:04.638
So we'll be able to
see you as clear as day.

00:33:04.670 --> 00:33:05.870
Are we good?

00:33:05.904 --> 00:33:07.037
Hair to the right.

00:33:07.070 --> 00:33:08.970
There, there.

00:33:09.004 --> 00:33:12.271
Michael: what do i do?

00:33:12.304 --> 00:33:15.904
Just stay under the covers.

00:33:15.937 --> 00:33:19.437
And if it shows up?

00:33:19.471 --> 00:33:21.337
Well, we'll be right in the next room.

00:33:21.371 --> 00:33:23.937
We're gonna come in with
guns, so as soon as we do,

00:33:23.970 --> 00:33:26.304
You roll off this bed
and you crawl under it.

00:33:28.371 --> 00:33:30.104
What if you shoot me?

00:33:30.137 --> 00:33:32.703
We won't shoot you. We're good shots.

00:33:34.337 --> 00:33:37.571
We're not gonna fire
until you're clear, okay?

00:33:37.604 --> 00:33:40.070
Have you heard a gunshot before?

00:33:40.104 --> 00:33:41.737
Like in the movies?

00:33:41.770 --> 00:33:45.337
It's gonna be a lot
louder than in the movies.

00:33:45.371 --> 00:33:48.970
So i want you to stay under
the bed, cover your ears,

00:33:49.004 --> 00:33:52.237
And do not come out until
we say so, you understand?

00:33:55.004 --> 00:33:57.837
Michael, are you sure
you want to do this?

00:33:57.870 --> 00:33:59.604
You don't have to. It's
okay. I won't be mad.

00:33:59.638 --> 00:34:01.638
No, i'm okay.

00:34:01.670 --> 00:34:04.471
Just don't shoot me.

00:34:04.504 --> 00:34:07.737
We're not gonna let
anything happen to you.

00:34:07.770 --> 00:34:09.070
I promise.

00:34:21.870 --> 00:34:23.237
What time is it?

00:34:25.337 --> 00:34:26.504
3:00.

00:34:28.538 --> 00:34:30.371
You sure these iron
rounds are gonna work?

00:34:32.337 --> 00:34:33.770
Consecrated iron rounds.

00:34:33.803 --> 00:34:37.437
And yeah, it's what dad used last time.

00:34:37.471 --> 00:34:40.171
Hey, dean, i'm sorry.

00:34:43.004 --> 00:34:44.070
For what?

00:34:46.703 --> 00:34:48.604
You know...

00:34:48.638 --> 00:34:51.737
I've really given you a lot of crap

00:34:51.770 --> 00:34:55.304
For always following dad's orders,

00:34:55.337 --> 00:34:58.803
But i know why you do it.

00:34:58.837 --> 00:35:00.837
Oh, god. Kill me now.

00:35:06.104 --> 00:35:07.171
Wait, look.

00:35:41.970 --> 00:35:43.604
Now? Not yet.

00:36:18.070 --> 00:36:19.604
Michael, down!

00:36:29.770 --> 00:36:31.471
Mike, you all right? Yeah.

00:36:31.504 --> 00:36:34.204
Just sit tight.

00:36:56.670 --> 00:36:57.703
Dean!

00:37:28.137 --> 00:37:30.037
Dean: hey!

00:37:33.137 --> 00:37:34.937
You okay, little brother?

00:38:07.504 --> 00:38:09.437
It's okay, michael. You can come on out.

00:38:41.977 --> 00:38:44.044
Hey, joanna, how's asher doing?

00:38:44.077 --> 00:38:46.111
Have you seen michael?
Michael: mom! Mom!

00:38:46.144 --> 00:38:47.744
Hey!

00:38:49.244 --> 00:38:50.443
How's ash?

00:38:50.477 --> 00:38:52.577
I've got some good news.
Your brother's gonna be fine.

00:38:52.610 --> 00:38:53.777
Really?

00:38:53.810 --> 00:38:55.777
Yeah, really. No one can explain it.

00:38:55.810 --> 00:38:58.644
It's, uh, it's a miracle.

00:38:58.677 --> 00:39:00.810
They're gonna keep him in
overnight for observation,

00:39:00.844 --> 00:39:02.311
But after that, he's coming home.

00:39:02.344 --> 00:39:03.378
That's great.

00:39:03.410 --> 00:39:05.911
How are all the other kids doing?

00:39:05.944 --> 00:39:07.144
Good, real good.

00:39:07.177 --> 00:39:09.244
A bunch of them should be
checking out in a few days.

00:39:09.278 --> 00:39:11.777
Dr. Travis says the ward's
gonna be like a ghost town.

00:39:11.810 --> 00:39:15.044
Dr. Travis? What about dr. Hydaker?

00:39:15.077 --> 00:39:16.144
Oh, he wasn't in today.

00:39:16.177 --> 00:39:17.877
He must have been sick or something.

00:39:17.911 --> 00:39:20.443
Yeah, yeah, must have.

00:39:20.477 --> 00:39:24.610
So did anything happen while i was gone?

00:39:24.644 --> 00:39:26.610
No, same old stuff.

00:39:26.644 --> 00:39:28.410
Okay. You can go see ash.

00:39:28.443 --> 00:39:29.944
Now? Only if you want to.

00:39:34.543 --> 00:39:35.810
I better get going

00:39:35.844 --> 00:39:38.077
Before he hot-Wires the
car and drives himself.

00:39:44.610 --> 00:39:48.311
It's too bad.

00:39:48.344 --> 00:39:50.944
No, they'll be fine.

00:39:50.977 --> 00:39:52.344
